network-streaming-telemetry is the vendor-neutral model-driven-streaming-telemetry skill: the push-based
counterpart to the poll-based paradigms in network-monitoring-selection. It owns the device-side transports
(gNMI, gNOI, NETCONF/YANG-push, Cisco MDT over OpenConfig or native YANG), subscription design (SAMPLE /
ON_CHANGE / TARGET_DEFINED, dial-in vs dial-out, encodings), and the receiver/collector tier (gnmic,
Telegraf gNMI + cisco_telemetry_mdt inputs, the OpenTelemetry gNMI/OpenConfig receiver, TLS/mTLS, pipeline
buffering/backpressure, scaling, hand-off to a TSDB/Kafka). Skill licensed Apache-2.0 (the primary-source
licence).

Scope + cadence (decided with the user at plan time, 2026-07-18 AskUserQuestion):
  - The 2026-05-21 disposition ("Network-telemetry-receivers + VPN": telemetry umbrella + extend
    vpn-tunnel-troubleshooting) reshaped against live disk. Flow (NetFlow / sFlow / IPFIX) is already
    DOUBLY owned (network-monitoring-selection design + kentik-network-monitoring engine), so the residual
    a new skill can own is the model-driven STREAMING-telemetry stack only.
  - User decision: CREATE a new narrow ops skill (not an nms extension), scoped to streaming telemetry +
    the receiver/collector tier. A minimal, user-sanctioned fifth-paradigm route-out was added to
    network-monitoring-selection (When-not-to-use + a Cross-references bullet); the nms four-paradigm core
    is unchanged.
  - Shape = design + ops umbrella with 3 references, per the network-monitoring-selection CREATE precedent.

